    "description": "The Integrated West Coast Pelagics Survey is a robust fisheries-independent survey that collects data that informs sustainable Pacific hake and coastal pelagic fisheries, gathers ecosystem data, and maintains the survey schedule. It integrates two coast-wide surveys into one efficient and economical survey. It will also use the latest advanced technology to sample effectively and employ artificial intelligence/machine learning to streamline data analyses. These technology advances rely heavily on cooperative research and collaboration with industry.  This experiment will contain the radiometric data collected during the surveys. Other data related to this cruise can be found HERE and for more information visit the NMFS_IWCPS website.",
